149
00:08:16,764 --> 00:08:20,568
If you ask me, that's something
worth dancing about.

150
00:08:20,601 --> 00:08:21,969
Ready, guys?

151
00:08:25,106 --> 00:08:26,207
Come on.

152
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,843
♪ You move your leg like this

153
00:08:28,876 --> 00:08:31,278
♪ And swing your arms
to the side ♪

154
00:08:31,312 --> 00:08:33,914
♪ And turn your head around

155
00:08:33,948 --> 00:08:36,617
♪ And you let your feet slide

156
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:37,852
♪ You do the Buddy glide

157
00:08:37,885 --> 00:08:39,153
♪ It's the Buddy glide

158
00:08:39,186 --> 00:08:40,588
♪ Do the Buddy glide

159
00:08:40,621 --> 00:08:42,056
♪ It's the Buddy glide

160
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,258
♪ To and fro, arms out wide

161
00:08:44,291 --> 00:08:45,693
♪ Don't run and hide

162
00:08:45,726 --> 00:08:47,194
♪ Do it with pride

163
00:08:47,228 --> 00:08:50,831
♪ That's how you do
the Buddy glide

164
00:08:50,865 --> 00:08:52,600
Woo-hoo-hoo!

165
00:08:52,633 --> 00:08:55,136
I am so proud of all of you.

166
00:08:55,169 --> 00:08:57,772
You put on an amazing show.

167
00:08:57,805 --> 00:09:00,741
And Josh learned
how to be brave.

168
00:09:00,775 --> 00:09:03,177
And now he's gonna be famous.

169
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:05,679
That's right, Trashy.

170
00:09:05,713 --> 00:09:09,183
Well, that's all the time
we have.

171
00:09:16,857 --> 00:09:20,628
♪ You love Buddy, yes, you do

172
00:09:20,661 --> 00:09:24,265
♪ And I love each one of you

173
00:09:24,298 --> 00:09:28,135
♪ We're together happily

174
00:09:28,169 --> 00:09:31,906
♪ We'll always be best buddies

175
00:09:31,939 --> 00:09:35,709
♪ I love every one of you

176
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:40,981
♪ I'm so glad you love me too ♪

177
00:09:51,092 --> 00:09:56,664
♪ He's a unicorn
from a magic land ♪

178
00:09:56,697 --> 00:10:01,302
♪ And we call his name
when we need a hand ♪

179
00:10:01,335 --> 00:10:06,841
♪ He's a pal
who knows our names ♪

180
00:10:06,874 --> 00:10:11,345
♪ He's the king
of fun and games ♪

181
00:10:12,713 --> 00:10:13,981
♪ It's Buddy

182
00:10:14,014 --> 00:10:15,249
♪ Oh, Buddy

183
00:10:15,282 --> 00:10:17,785
♪ Our friend until the end

184
00:10:17,818 --> 00:10:21,422
♪ It's Buddy ♪

185
00:10:25,726 --> 00:10:28,896
One, two, three.

186
00:10:28,929 --> 00:10:30,197
Three, five.

187
00:10:31,966 --> 00:10:34,034
Oh, no. I was winning!

188
00:10:34,068 --> 00:10:36,170
Well, no wonder
you're sneezing.

189
00:10:36,203 --> 00:10:38,239
Look at these dust bunnies.

190
00:10:38,272 --> 00:10:41,375
I'd like to be
the only bunny here, thank you.

191
00:10:41,408 --> 00:10:42,943
Hi! I'm Hannah.

192
00:10:42,977 --> 00:10:45,446
I love to sing and dance!

193
00:10:45,479 --> 00:10:46,515
Hi, Hannah.

194
00:10:46,548 --> 00:10:49,150
Looks like we came
at the right time.

195
00:10:49,183 --> 00:10:51,218
We have some cleaning to do.

196
00:10:51,252 --> 00:10:53,053
Do we have to clean now?

197
00:10:53,087 --> 00:10:54,722
We're in the middle
of playing our game,

198
00:10:54,755 --> 00:10:57,358
and cleaning doesn't seem
very fun.

199
00:10:57,391 --> 00:10:59,960
I know someone
who can make it fun.

200
00:10:59,994 --> 00:11:01,328
-Oh, Budd--
-Wait.

201
00:11:01,362 --> 00:11:05,833
Uh, you guys get Buddy
while Wade and I,

202
00:11:05,866 --> 00:11:07,935
we'll go get the vacuum.

203
00:11:14,509 --> 00:11:15,409
What is it, Freddy?

204
00:11:15,442 --> 00:11:16,911
Are we gonna vacuum the grass?

205
00:11:16,944 --> 00:11:18,212
Look.

206
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,215
Josh's book?

207
00:11:21,248 --> 00:11:22,983
I found it in the trash.

208
00:11:23,017 --> 00:11:25,386
Look, it's stained.

209
00:11:25,419 --> 00:11:27,755
It looks like blood.

210
00:11:30,257 --> 00:11:32,393
Hey, Mr. Mailbox,
can you mail this to Josh

211
00:11:32,426 --> 00:11:33,360
in Diamond City for me?

212
00:11:35,829 --> 00:11:38,399
Mr. Mailbox.

213
00:11:38,432 --> 00:11:41,101
What happened to your door?

214
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:43,871
Hi, Wade. Hi, Freddy.

215
00:11:45,806 --> 00:11:48,075
What's that you have there,
Wade?

216
00:11:51,946 --> 00:11:53,781
Josh's book.

217
00:11:53,814 --> 00:11:55,783
I've been looking for this.

218
00:11:55,816 --> 00:11:57,318
I'll get it to Josh.

219
00:11:57,351 --> 00:11:59,086
Freddy found it in the trash.

220
00:11:59,119 --> 00:12:01,755
It has stains on it.

221
00:12:01,789 --> 00:12:03,525
Oh, that's right.

222
00:12:03,558 --> 00:12:06,493
I was painting a goodbye card
for Josh,

223
00:12:06,528 --> 00:12:09,763
and Betty spilled red paint
on his book.

224
00:12:09,797 --> 00:12:14,001
So, I got him a new book
and I threw this away.

225
00:12:14,034 --> 00:12:15,769
Now I remember.

226
00:12:19,373 --> 00:12:20,508
Buddy?

227
00:12:20,542 --> 00:12:22,776
What is it, Freddy?

228
00:12:22,810 --> 00:12:24,945
Can we send Josh
a goodbye card too?

229
00:12:24,979 --> 00:12:27,147
Of course you can.

230
00:12:27,181 --> 00:12:30,351
But, first, it's time
to learn about cleaning.

231
00:12:30,384 --> 00:12:31,819
Cleaning is important.

232
00:12:31,852 --> 00:12:34,255
It kills germs
and it keeps us healthy.

233
00:12:34,288 --> 00:12:36,524
Different jobs
need different cleaners.

234
00:12:36,558 --> 00:12:38,192
Dishes need detergent.

235
00:12:38,225 --> 00:12:40,294
Windows need window cleaner.

236
00:12:40,327 --> 00:12:42,429
Some cleaners
are very poisonous.

237
00:12:42,463 --> 00:12:45,032
Some can catch fire
very easily.

238
00:12:45,065 --> 00:12:47,468
Always ask a grown-up
before handling chemicals

239
00:12:47,502 --> 00:12:49,470
under the sink.

240
00:12:49,504 --> 00:12:52,139
Now, let's get cleaning!

241
00:13:00,881 --> 00:13:02,983
Wade, I'm scared.

242
00:13:03,017 --> 00:13:04,985
I can't stop thinking
about Josh's book.

243
00:13:05,019 --> 00:13:06,287
Seriously, Freddy?

244
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,289
He loved that book.

245
00:13:08,322 --> 00:13:11,325
And the stains
didn't look like paint.

246
00:13:11,358 --> 00:13:12,192
Of course it's paint.

247
00:13:12,226 --> 00:13:14,128
-Why would Buddy lie?
-He wouldn't.

248
00:13:14,161 --> 00:13:16,063
That's what I keep telling her.

249
00:13:17,632 --> 00:13:20,434
Betty, I have
a cleaning question.

250
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:22,202
What did you use
to clean up the paint

251
00:13:22,236 --> 00:13:23,605
you spilled on Josh's card?

252
00:13:23,638 --> 00:13:25,906
I never made Josh a card.

253
00:13:25,939 --> 00:13:28,375
And I certainly
never spill paint.

254
00:13:28,409 --> 00:13:30,010
Hm!

255
00:13:32,547 --> 00:13:34,148
Wade, I'm scared.

256
00:13:39,587 --> 00:13:40,988
Why would Buddy lie?

257
00:13:41,021 --> 00:13:42,022
I don't know.

258
00:13:42,056 --> 00:13:44,258
We need to talk to an adult
like Nurse Nancy.

259
00:13:44,291 --> 00:13:46,894
But we're supposed to be
cleaning.

260
00:13:46,927 --> 00:13:48,329
I have an idea.

261
00:13:48,362 --> 00:13:51,165
Great work, gang.

262
00:13:51,198 --> 00:13:54,569
How about a song
to really make it sparkle?

263
00:13:59,073 --> 00:14:01,408
♪ It's time to clean,
clean, clean ♪

264
00:14:01,442 --> 00:14:03,477
♪ Find where the dusty things
lurk ♪

265
00:14:05,145 --> 00:14:07,948
♪ And soon it will gleam,
gleam, gleam ♪

266
00:14:07,981 --> 00:14:10,417
♪ 'Cause many hands
make light work ♪

267
00:14:10,451 --> 00:14:12,453
Ouch!

268
00:14:12,486 --> 00:14:14,388
♪ I've got a splinter
in my finger

269
00:14:14,421 --> 00:14:16,423
and it couldn't hurt worse ♪

270
00:14:16,457 --> 00:14:19,661
♪ Better not linger
and go see the nurse ♪

271
00:14:19,694 --> 00:14:23,330
♪ Before it gets worse,
you need to go see a nurse ♪

272
00:14:23,364 --> 00:14:26,467
♪ Go to the nurse,
go to the nurse ♪

273
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:32,574
♪ Before it gets worse,
you need to go to the nurse

274
00:14:32,607 --> 00:14:34,208
Well, gosh.

275
00:14:34,241 --> 00:14:36,678
I thought we were singing
about cleaning.

276
00:14:36,711 --> 00:14:38,546
I better go see Nurse Nancy.

277
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,047
It could get infected.

278
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,115
Safety first.

279
00:14:41,148 --> 00:14:42,349
Like you always say, Buddy.

280
00:14:42,383 --> 00:14:45,319
You do always say that.

281
00:14:45,352 --> 00:14:48,922
Uh-huh. I guess I do.

282
00:14:48,956 --> 00:14:50,090
I'll go with him.

283
00:14:55,462 --> 00:14:58,298
Hi, Freddy. Hi, Wade.
Hi, Strappy.

284
00:14:58,332 --> 00:14:59,534
How can I help you?

285
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:04,238
Guess I wasn't paying attention
and I got a splinter.

286
00:15:04,271 --> 00:15:06,039
Hmm.

287
00:15:06,073 --> 00:15:08,275
I don't see a splinter.

288
00:15:08,308 --> 00:15:10,411
There isn't a splinter.

289
00:15:10,444 --> 00:15:12,246
We were just pretending.

290
00:15:12,279 --> 00:15:13,681
Why would you do that?

291
00:15:13,715 --> 00:15:16,651
We wanted to ask you something.

292
00:15:16,684 --> 00:15:20,154
Have you noticed anything weird
about Buddy lately?

293
00:15:20,187 --> 00:15:21,623
I don't know what you mean.

294
00:15:21,656 --> 00:15:24,291
We found Josh's book
in the trash.

295
00:15:24,324 --> 00:15:25,259
It had blood on it.

296
00:15:25,292 --> 00:15:28,228
Buddy said that Betty
spilled red paint on it,

297
00:15:28,262 --> 00:15:31,064
but Betty said that she didn't.

298
00:15:31,098 --> 00:15:33,300
Betty does get confused.

299
00:15:34,702 --> 00:15:37,739
Um, I'll tell you what.

300
00:15:37,772 --> 00:15:39,406
I'll talk to Buddy.

301
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:43,511
I'm sure there's a reasonable
explanation for all of this.

302
00:15:48,015 --> 00:15:49,517
♪ Together ♪

303
00:15:49,551 --> 00:15:51,385
Where are you going?

304
00:15:51,418 --> 00:15:54,154
I want to hear what Buddy's
gonna say to Nurse Nancy.

305
00:15:56,256 --> 00:15:58,560
-That's eavesdropping.
-Don't be such a goody-goody.

306
00:15:58,593 --> 00:16:00,160
What's wrong
with being a goody-goody?

307
00:16:00,194 --> 00:16:01,261
Better than being a snoop.

308
00:16:01,295 --> 00:16:03,330
-Zip it, Strappy.
-Okay.

309
00:16:11,739 --> 00:16:13,541
Guess everything's fine.

310
00:16:15,142 --> 00:16:16,443
Yeah, everything's fine.

311
00:16:16,477 --> 00:16:19,079
Look how tightly
he's hugging her neck.

312
00:16:48,810 --> 00:16:50,444
-Did he see you?
-I don't know.

313
00:16:50,477 --> 00:16:52,379
Come on. We have to tell
the others.

314
00:16:54,014 --> 00:16:58,118
♪ Chores can be fun
when you do them together ♪

315
00:16:58,151 --> 00:16:59,821
♪ It's not hard...

316
00:16:59,854 --> 00:17:01,723
Guys! Guys! Guys!

317
00:17:01,756 --> 00:17:03,323
♪ A little dusting
and scrubbing ♪

318
00:17:03,357 --> 00:17:04,424
Hannah.

319
00:17:04,458 --> 00:17:05,627
-Oliver!
-Oliver!

320
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:07,494
♪ When friends share the load,

321
00:17:07,529 --> 00:17:10,297
the work is a breeze

322
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:14,569
So fun!

323
00:17:14,602 --> 00:17:16,169
Don't go in the clubhouse.

324
00:17:16,203 --> 00:17:17,805
I just mopped.

325
00:17:19,373 --> 00:17:21,275
What did you want to say,
Freddy?

326
00:17:21,308 --> 00:17:24,679
That we just love cleaning
so much.

327
00:17:24,712 --> 00:17:28,215
Well, that's all the time
we have.

328
00:17:35,657 --> 00:17:39,459
♪ You love Buddy, yes, you do

329
00:17:39,493 --> 00:17:43,363
♪ And I love each one of you

330
00:17:43,397 --> 00:17:47,167
♪ We're together happily

331
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,805
♪ We'll always be best buddies

332
00:17:50,838 --> 00:17:54,609
♪ I love every one of you

333
00:17:54,642 --> 00:17:59,514
♪ I'm so glad you love me too ♪

334
00:18:07,822 --> 00:18:09,724
♪ Friends until the end

335
00:18:09,757 --> 00:18:13,528
♪ It's Buddy ♪

336
00:18:19,299 --> 00:18:20,868
I'm so nervous.

337
00:18:20,902 --> 00:18:22,169
It's Buddy's birthday,

338
00:18:22,202 --> 00:18:24,471
and I want everything
to be perfect,

339
00:18:24,505 --> 00:18:27,407
but my gift hasn't arrived
from Diamond City.

340
00:18:27,441 --> 00:18:28,576
Don't worry, Betty.

341
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:30,778
Charlie the Train
is always on time.

342
00:18:30,812 --> 00:18:34,414
And he's due right about now.

343
00:18:36,851 --> 00:18:38,786
Charlie the Train!

344
00:18:43,658 --> 00:18:45,693
Hello, kids!

345
00:18:48,328 --> 00:18:52,265
Special delivery
from Diamond City.

346
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:53,801
Charlie the Train.

347
00:18:53,835 --> 00:18:56,838
And, boy,
are my wheels tuckered.

348
00:18:56,871 --> 00:18:58,640
Oh, thank goodness.

349
00:18:58,673 --> 00:19:00,675
Now we need to put up
the decorations and--

350
00:19:01,743 --> 00:19:04,311
I don't even know
what kind of cake he likes.

351
00:19:05,212 --> 00:19:08,382
Well, why don't we ask him?

352
00:19:08,415 --> 00:19:09,651
-Oh...
-Wait!

353
00:19:09,684 --> 00:19:12,754
-We can't bring him here yet.
-Why not?

354
00:19:12,787 --> 00:19:15,957
Because it's
a surprise birthday party.

355
00:19:15,990 --> 00:19:18,225
Surprise party?

356
00:19:18,258 --> 00:19:20,460
What a great idea!

357
00:19:20,494 --> 00:19:21,629
We better get to work before--

358
00:19:21,663 --> 00:19:23,230
Don't say his name.

359
00:19:23,263 --> 00:19:24,464
Don't even think it.

360
00:19:24,498 --> 00:19:26,233
Not until we're ready.

361
00:19:26,266 --> 00:19:28,770
Just say "B-word" for now.

362
00:19:28,803 --> 00:19:29,904
That's fun.

363
00:19:29,937 --> 00:19:34,709
Then I better get B-word's
present for the clubhouse.

364
00:19:39,847 --> 00:19:42,550
Wait, Oliver, Hannah,

365
00:19:42,583 --> 00:19:43,851
can we talk to you
for a minute?

366
00:19:43,885 --> 00:19:46,286
Of course. What's up?

367
00:19:47,855 --> 00:19:49,423
Not here.

368
00:19:56,564 --> 00:19:58,298
There's something going on
with B-word.

369
00:19:58,331 --> 00:19:59,399
What do you mean?

370
00:19:59,433 --> 00:20:00,802
-Is he sick?
-Yes.

371
00:20:00,835 --> 00:20:02,870
But not like a cold.

372
00:20:02,904 --> 00:20:04,772
Like...

373
00:20:04,806 --> 00:20:05,673
In the head.

374
00:20:05,707 --> 00:20:07,374
He is kind of silly sometimes.

375
00:20:07,407 --> 00:20:08,776
He killed Nurse Nancy.

376
00:20:12,046 --> 00:20:14,015
That's not a funny joke.

377
00:20:14,048 --> 00:20:15,282
It's not a joke.

378
00:20:15,315 --> 00:20:17,250
We saw him do it.

379
00:20:17,284 --> 00:20:19,821
And we think he did it
to Josh, too.

380
00:20:19,854 --> 00:20:21,488
You guys are being mean.

381
00:20:21,522 --> 00:20:22,523
B-word loves us!

382
00:20:22,557 --> 00:20:23,390
What do you know, Hannah?

383
00:20:23,423 --> 00:20:25,927
You just got here.

384
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,929
I'm sorry, guys, it's true.

385
00:20:27,962 --> 00:20:29,731
I saw it too.

386
00:20:29,764 --> 00:20:31,566
We need to go to Diamond City.

387
00:20:31,599 --> 00:20:32,834
Leave the park?

388
00:20:32,867 --> 00:20:35,636
But B-word says it's not safe
out there without a grown-up.

389
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:37,337
Wait. Stop talking. Look!

390
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,273
Do you think
he heard us talking?

391
00:20:40,307 --> 00:20:41,308
Is he gonna come to life?

392
00:20:41,341 --> 00:20:42,777
But I didn't do anything wrong.

393
00:20:42,810 --> 00:20:44,277
We can't keep him away forever.

394
00:20:44,311 --> 00:20:45,947
We need to walk calmly
to the train.

395
00:20:53,821 --> 00:20:55,890
-Hey, kids.
-Hi, Mailman Miles.

396
00:20:55,923 --> 00:20:57,525
See you at the party, right?

397
00:21:02,663 --> 00:21:03,497
Wait.

398
00:21:04,799 --> 00:21:06,934
B-word is on the swings now.

399
00:21:06,968 --> 00:21:08,335
Keep walking.

400
00:21:08,368 --> 00:21:09,469
Don't look at it.

401
00:21:15,777 --> 00:21:16,978
Oh, Buddy!

402
00:21:18,679 --> 00:21:20,380
Hi, Oliver!

403
00:21:20,413 --> 00:21:21,983
What's wrong?

404
00:21:22,016 --> 00:21:23,584
We need to hurry.

405
00:21:26,988 --> 00:21:29,657
Hey, Charlie, we need to go
to Diamond City right now!

406
00:21:29,690 --> 00:21:32,492
-But you'll miss Buddy's party.
-It's an emergency.

407
00:21:32,527 --> 00:21:34,562
I'm really sick.

408
00:21:34,595 --> 00:21:35,530
Oh, no.

409
00:21:35,563 --> 00:21:36,496
Okay, then.

410
00:21:36,531 --> 00:21:37,565
All aboard!

411
00:21:40,067 --> 00:21:43,403
Next stop, Diamond City!

412
00:21:48,576 --> 00:21:50,812
Hi, guys, what are you doing?

413
00:21:50,845 --> 00:21:52,345
Clear the track, Buddy.

414
00:21:52,379 --> 00:21:55,750
Wade is sick and I gotta
get him to Diamond City.

415
00:21:55,783 --> 00:21:56,951
No, Charlie.

416
00:21:56,984 --> 00:21:58,820
I'll take him to the nurse.

417
00:21:58,853 --> 00:22:00,487
You murdered the nurse, Buddy.

418
00:22:00,521 --> 00:22:02,623
Wade, you know that's a lie.

419
00:22:02,657 --> 00:22:04,692
And lying is very bad.

420
00:22:04,725 --> 00:22:06,727
I don't want to be
in the middle of this.

421
00:22:06,761 --> 00:22:08,963
Get out of the train, Wade.

422
00:22:08,996 --> 00:22:10,932
I'll take you to the nurse.

423
00:22:10,965 --> 00:22:13,100
No.

424
00:22:13,134 --> 00:22:14,602
Really, Wade?

425
00:22:14,635 --> 00:22:16,938
On my birthday?

426
00:22:16,971 --> 00:22:19,140
I'll take you to the nurse
right now.

427
00:22:19,173 --> 00:22:21,374
If she says you need
to go to Diamond City,

428
00:22:21,408 --> 00:22:23,443
you go to Diamond City.

429
00:22:23,476 --> 00:22:24,377
Bring the nurse here.

430
00:22:24,411 --> 00:22:26,047
That sounds like a good idea.

431
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,415
Bring Nurse Nancy here.

432
00:22:38,526 --> 00:22:41,062
Buddy, you promised
you wouldn't be mad.

433
00:22:41,095 --> 00:22:42,997
Go back into the clubhouse,
Oliver.

434
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:45,533
This does not concern you.

435
00:22:48,870 --> 00:22:52,506
Everybody,
back into the clubhouse now!

436
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,516
Not you, Wade.

437
00:23:02,550 --> 00:23:04,619
I need to talk to you.

438
00:23:04,652 --> 00:23:07,088
You lied about me,
and you hurt my feelings.

439
00:23:07,121 --> 00:23:08,656
Buddy, please.

440
00:23:08,689 --> 00:23:09,924
Don't worry, Freddy.

441
00:23:09,957 --> 00:23:11,893
I know Wade was responsible.

442
00:23:11,926 --> 00:23:13,895
Now go inside.

443
00:23:13,928 --> 00:23:15,495
Come on, Freddy.

444
00:23:20,601 --> 00:23:22,737
-Betty.
-There you are.

445
00:23:22,770 --> 00:23:24,038
Hurry and put that sign up.

446
00:23:24,071 --> 00:23:25,773
Buddy will be here soon.

447
00:23:25,806 --> 00:23:28,843
-He's going to kill Wade.
-What?

448
00:23:28,876 --> 00:23:31,045
Buddy's going to kill Wade.

449
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:34,115
We better hide.

450
00:23:34,148 --> 00:23:35,850
Buddy will be here soon.

451
00:23:44,558 --> 00:23:46,227
What are you doing, Freddy?

452
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:48,029
We're not supposed to mess
with the chemicals

453
00:23:48,062 --> 00:23:49,964
under the sink.

454
00:23:49,997 --> 00:23:51,632
No. Freddy.

455
00:23:51,666 --> 00:23:53,834
Buddy is too powerful.

456
00:24:03,210 --> 00:24:04,745
Why are you cutting yourself,
Wade?

457
00:24:04,779 --> 00:24:06,614
Please, no! Ow!

458
00:24:06,647 --> 00:24:08,649
Stop cutting yourself.

459
00:24:08,683 --> 00:24:09,784
I don't want you to get hurt.

460
00:24:12,553 --> 00:24:16,190
You better put down
the knife, Wade.

461
00:24:16,223 --> 00:24:17,692
Whoa!

462
00:24:19,226 --> 00:24:20,995
What are you doing, Freddy?

463
00:24:21,028 --> 00:24:23,798
I told you to stay in the cl--

464
00:24:23,831 --> 00:24:25,533
A lighter?

465
00:24:25,566 --> 00:24:28,002
Freddy, this isn't like you.

466
00:24:28,035 --> 00:24:30,571
This is crazy.

467
00:24:30,604 --> 00:24:32,707
Drop the lighter, Freddy.

468
00:24:34,008 --> 00:24:36,077
Drop the lighter, Freddy.

469
00:24:39,647 --> 00:24:41,649
That's better.

470
00:24:41,682 --> 00:24:43,751
Now go back in the clubhouse.

471
00:24:43,784 --> 00:24:47,088
A lighter
is a very dangerous thing.

472
00:24:47,121 --> 00:24:47,955
You have to be--

473
00:25:11,212 --> 00:25:12,880
Buddy?

474
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:20,921
Buddy?

475
00:25:23,124 --> 00:25:26,560
Well, that's all the time
we have.

476
00:25:28,729 --> 00:25:30,631
Come hug me, kids.

477
00:25:30,664 --> 00:25:33,334
Buddy, let's get you
to the nurse, okay?

478
00:25:35,036 --> 00:25:36,303
Just give me the knife.

479
00:25:36,337 --> 00:25:37,571
You want the knife?

480
00:25:37,605 --> 00:25:38,739
Here's the knife.

481
00:25:40,641 --> 00:25:42,743
It's nice to share.

482
00:25:47,848 --> 00:25:51,218
Kids, it's okay.

483
00:25:51,252 --> 00:25:54,021
I'm not mad.

484
00:25:54,055 --> 00:25:56,690
Everybody needs to calm down.

485
00:25:59,126 --> 00:26:04,231
Kids, I want you to come out
on the count of three, okay?

486
00:26:05,966 --> 00:26:08,335
One.

487
00:26:08,369 --> 00:26:09,737
Two.

488
00:26:13,074 --> 00:26:15,376
Two and three quarters.

489
00:26:16,977 --> 00:26:19,680
Wait, Mr. Mailbox!

490
00:26:19,713 --> 00:26:21,816
Two and four-fifths!

491
00:26:21,849 --> 00:26:23,284
Hannah, come help me!

492
00:26:23,317 --> 00:26:26,153
You can't hide forever.

493
00:26:26,187 --> 00:26:27,888
Two and five-sixths.

494
00:26:27,922 --> 00:26:30,091
Um, do we really have to take
Mr. Mailbox?

495
00:26:30,124 --> 00:26:31,392
No offense, Mr. Mailbox.

496
00:26:31,425 --> 00:26:32,827
Three!

497
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:35,963
Ready or not, here I come.

498
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:52,046
It's okay.
It's how mistakes happen.

499
00:26:52,079 --> 00:26:55,816
But friends stick together,
right?

500
00:26:57,017 --> 00:26:58,419
-Right?
-Come on, Hannah!

501
00:27:00,254 --> 00:27:01,989
-Come on.
-It is dangerous

502
00:27:02,022 --> 00:27:03,190
outside the park.

503
00:27:03,224 --> 00:27:05,226
There are monsters out there.

504
00:27:05,259 --> 00:27:07,027
You're the monster, Buddy.

505
00:27:07,061 --> 00:27:08,996
You're hurting my feelings.

506
00:27:10,898 --> 00:27:12,733
Don't leave me!

507
00:27:12,766 --> 00:27:14,735
Hurry, Freddy!

508
00:27:15,936 --> 00:27:17,438
Wade, come on.

509
00:27:23,410 --> 00:27:26,013
Pull me up, Freddy!

510
00:27:26,046 --> 00:27:28,349
I'm trying.

511
00:27:29,250 --> 00:27:31,685
Freddy, help!

512
00:27:35,055 --> 00:27:36,924
I see you.

513
00:27:47,768 --> 00:27:48,969
Come on, Wade.

514
00:27:49,003 --> 00:27:51,338
Well, that's all the time
we have.

515
00:27:51,372 --> 00:27:54,008
♪ You love Buddy, yes, you do

516
00:27:54,041 --> 00:27:58,245
♪ And I love each one of you

517
00:27:58,279 --> 00:28:00,147
It's not working.

518
00:28:00,181 --> 00:28:03,117
♪ We're together happily

519
00:28:03,150 --> 00:28:06,287
♪ We'll always be
best buddies

520
00:28:37,418 --> 00:28:39,220
Uh-huh.

521
00:28:39,253 --> 00:28:40,788
Yeah.

522
00:28:40,821 --> 00:28:42,423
Sure, yes.

523
00:28:42,456 --> 00:28:44,526
Uh, well, we can work
with a, uh,

524
00:28:44,559 --> 00:28:48,896
a whole variety of budgets
to fit any project, yeah.

525
00:28:48,929 --> 00:28:51,098
Yes, absolutely.

526
00:28:51,131 --> 00:28:52,233
Mom!

527
00:28:53,968 --> 00:28:57,304
Oh, uh, Diane,
can I call you right back?

528
00:28:57,338 --> 00:28:59,173
Okay. All right, thank you.

529
00:29:03,244 --> 00:29:05,446
But what if that one falls off?

530
00:29:05,479 --> 00:29:08,048
Well, that's why I use two.

531
00:29:08,082 --> 00:29:10,484
So they can look out
for each other.

532
00:29:17,925 --> 00:29:20,060
Oh, my God, okay.

533
00:29:20,094 --> 00:29:21,228
Okay, let's go.

534
00:29:21,262 --> 00:29:22,096
I gotta go get your brother.

535
00:29:22,129 --> 00:29:23,397
Let's go.

536
00:29:24,398 --> 00:29:25,899
Hi!

537
00:29:25,933 --> 00:29:27,034
I'm so sorry I'm late.

538
00:29:27,067 --> 00:29:29,136
Sorry, thank you.

539
00:29:29,169 --> 00:29:31,238
Good to see you.

540
00:29:31,272 --> 00:29:33,907
Sorry I'm late.

541
00:29:33,941 --> 00:29:35,809
How was the party?

542
00:29:35,843 --> 00:29:37,111
Fine.

543
00:29:39,146 --> 00:29:41,282
What is that?
Is that a goldfish?

544
00:29:41,315 --> 00:29:42,584
Everyone got one.

545
00:29:42,617 --> 00:29:44,485
For going to the party,
I guess.

546
00:29:44,519 --> 00:29:45,986
Oh, wow.

547
00:29:47,154 --> 00:29:48,856
You know, in my day,

548
00:29:48,889 --> 00:29:52,026
just the birthday kid
got presents.

549
00:29:54,261 --> 00:29:56,163
Maybe this will be fun.

550
00:29:56,196 --> 00:29:58,299
What was the name
of the goldfish you had before?

551
00:29:58,332 --> 00:30:00,801
-I never had a goldfish.
-Yes, you did.

552
00:30:02,169 --> 00:30:05,039
Oh, maybe it was a betta fish.

553
00:30:05,072 --> 00:30:07,274
Oh, my gosh,
you loved that fish,

554
00:30:07,308 --> 00:30:09,276
but then you said
that you wanted a pet

555
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:11,312
you could actually pet.

556
00:30:11,345 --> 00:30:13,280
Do you remember that?

557
00:30:13,314 --> 00:30:15,182
Was I a baby or something?

558
00:30:16,618 --> 00:30:18,052
No.

559
00:30:20,487 --> 00:30:21,989
No.

560
00:30:22,022 --> 00:30:23,490
Maybe it was Timothy?

561
00:30:25,893 --> 00:30:28,896
I mean, who does that?

562
00:30:28,929 --> 00:30:31,098
Gives a kid a fish?

563
00:30:31,131 --> 00:30:32,132
Without asking?

564
00:30:32,166 --> 00:30:34,435
It's like, who's gonna clean it?

565
00:30:35,936 --> 00:30:38,005
I will.

566
00:30:38,038 --> 00:30:39,473
Bud, you don't even clean
your room.

567
00:30:39,507 --> 00:30:40,874
Yeah, I do.

568
00:30:40,908 --> 00:30:42,176
I just did clean my room.

569
00:30:42,209 --> 00:30:44,144
Guys, dinner, come on!

570
00:30:46,413 --> 00:30:48,949
Derek, no headphones, honey.

571
00:30:48,982 --> 00:30:50,217
-It's just one.
-But our dinner

572
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:51,251
doesn't need a soundtrack.

573
00:30:51,285 --> 00:30:54,054
Our lively conversation
is enough.

574
00:30:55,590 --> 00:30:57,424
Come on, everybody!

575
00:30:59,126 --> 00:31:01,596
We're literally all here.

576
00:31:03,430 --> 00:31:05,199
Let's dig in.

577
00:31:05,232 --> 00:31:07,901
Ooh, what do you guys got?
Nuggets.

578
00:31:07,935 --> 00:31:11,138
"Imagine whirled peas."

579
00:31:12,473 --> 00:31:13,641
Get it?

580
00:31:13,675 --> 00:31:16,076
'Cause it sounds
like "world peace."

581
00:31:16,110 --> 00:31:18,245
-I don't get it.
-"Whirled peas"

582
00:31:18,278 --> 00:31:20,280
sounds like "world peace."

583
00:31:20,314 --> 00:31:22,282
But what are whirled peas?

584
00:31:22,316 --> 00:31:24,586
I mean, is that really a food?

585
00:31:24,619 --> 00:31:26,453
Is it really?

586
00:31:26,487 --> 00:31:28,623
Yeah, it's peas in a blender,
something like mashed potatoes.

587
00:31:28,656 --> 00:31:31,291
I don't know, it's just
a funny bumper sticker I saw.

588
00:31:31,325 --> 00:31:32,694
But people don't eat that.

589
00:31:32,727 --> 00:31:34,662
Not a food, is it?

590
00:31:34,696 --> 00:31:36,363
Well, maybe it's not a food,

591
00:31:36,397 --> 00:31:38,600
but it's not like
you can't whirl a pea.

592
00:31:46,608 --> 00:31:48,475
-Doesn't make sense to me.
-Look, guys,

593
00:31:48,510 --> 00:31:51,178
puns don't have to be
literal, okay?

594
00:31:58,252 --> 00:31:59,587
Honey?

595
00:32:10,397 --> 00:32:13,033
She's fine, thank God.

596
00:32:13,066 --> 00:32:15,402
Mom just had a little something
going on with her stomach,

597
00:32:15,436 --> 00:32:16,704
but she's better now.

598
00:32:16,738 --> 00:32:18,640
Why don't you try
to get to sleep, okay?

599
00:32:18,673 --> 00:32:20,642
Goodnight.

600
00:32:32,286 --> 00:32:34,221
-Hey.
-Hi.

601
00:32:35,723 --> 00:32:38,192
I am so sorry about that!

602
00:32:38,225 --> 00:32:39,761
No, come on, it's okay,

603
00:32:39,794 --> 00:32:41,563
just walk me through it again.

604
00:32:41,596 --> 00:32:45,098
You said the chair was...
cursed?

605
00:32:45,132 --> 00:32:46,534
No.

606
00:32:46,568 --> 00:32:48,503
It just, uh...

607
00:32:53,173 --> 00:32:55,976
It was the worst feeling
I've ever felt.

608
00:32:57,444 --> 00:33:01,783
Just an icy-cold...

609
00:33:01,816 --> 00:33:03,116
hole.

610
00:33:03,150 --> 00:33:04,351
Oh.

611
00:33:06,053 --> 00:33:07,755
We'll move the chair.

612
00:33:07,789 --> 00:33:08,823
We hardly use it, anyway.

613
00:33:08,857 --> 00:33:10,357
-We'll just move it.
-It's not about the chair.

614
00:33:10,390 --> 00:33:12,760
Okay, then, uh,
we won't move the chair.

615
00:33:12,794 --> 00:33:15,262
The important thing is,

616
00:33:15,295 --> 00:33:17,197
you feel better now, right?

617
00:33:20,067 --> 00:33:21,569
No, I don't.

618
00:33:27,307 --> 00:33:28,510
I'm sorry.

619
00:33:30,612 --> 00:33:32,379
Oof!

620
00:33:32,412 --> 00:33:34,281
Gonna look for a therapist
tomorrow.

621
00:33:34,314 --> 00:33:36,618
-Oh! There you go.
-Yeah.

622
00:33:36,651 --> 00:33:38,653
What a great idea.

623
00:33:38,686 --> 00:33:40,287
Yeah.

624
00:33:40,320 --> 00:33:42,256
Therapist.

625
00:33:42,289 --> 00:33:43,490
Good thinking.

626
00:33:47,327 --> 00:33:48,495
By the way.

627
00:33:50,230 --> 00:33:52,132
I don't think there's
anything embarrassing

628
00:33:52,165 --> 00:33:53,166
about self-care.

629
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:54,569
Oh yeah, neither do I.

630
00:33:54,602 --> 00:33:56,436
Exactly.

631
00:33:56,470 --> 00:33:58,405
All right.

632
00:34:07,214 --> 00:34:08,415
Seat belt.

633
00:34:25,867 --> 00:34:28,168
Mom! What are you doing?

634
00:34:28,201 --> 00:34:29,871
Yeah. Sorry.

635
00:34:29,904 --> 00:34:31,873
The empty chair
could represent a feeling

636
00:34:31,906 --> 00:34:35,342
of absence or loss.

637
00:34:35,375 --> 00:34:37,377
Why do you think
you might feel that way?

638
00:34:39,479 --> 00:34:41,181
I don't know.

639
00:34:41,214 --> 00:34:43,751
How's the relationship
with your husband?

640
00:34:43,785 --> 00:34:47,254
Fine. It's good.

641
00:34:47,287 --> 00:34:49,389
Do you think
that I can get meds?

642
00:34:51,458 --> 00:34:54,796
Well, that's one of the tools
we have at our disposal, but...

643
00:34:54,829 --> 00:34:56,330
Mm-hm.

644
00:34:56,363 --> 00:34:58,566
I'd like to go a little deeper,

645
00:34:58,600 --> 00:35:01,536
maybe hear how you're feeling.

646
00:35:07,207 --> 00:35:08,576
Grace?

647
00:35:16,183 --> 00:35:17,384
Grace?

648
00:35:29,631 --> 00:35:31,298
Well, it's not about the time

649
00:35:31,331 --> 00:35:33,868
but about the money
and your grades.

650
00:35:33,901 --> 00:35:35,770
We had a deal, remember?

651
00:35:35,803 --> 00:35:37,204
I already promised
Nate and Chris

652
00:35:37,237 --> 00:35:38,372
that I'm going, though.

653
00:35:38,405 --> 00:35:40,875
Okay, so, that's my fault?

654
00:35:49,216 --> 00:35:50,283
Good evening.

655
00:35:50,317 --> 00:35:51,519
I'm Dr. Deborah Burr.

656
00:35:51,552 --> 00:35:53,788
-You must be Grace.
-Yes. You're early.

657
00:35:53,821 --> 00:35:57,290
I sensed a greater urgency.

658
00:35:59,259 --> 00:36:02,730
Hi. Uh...sorry, uh,
who's this?

659
00:36:02,764 --> 00:36:04,899
Uh, this is Dr. Deborah Burr...

660
00:36:04,932 --> 00:36:07,735
-Clairvoyant parapsychologist.
-...and she's a...um...

661
00:36:10,237 --> 00:36:11,539
So, you hired a psychic?

662
00:36:11,572 --> 00:36:13,574
-You must be Ben.
-Oh, okay.

663
00:36:13,608 --> 00:36:15,308
Did your powers
tell you that?

664
00:36:16,476 --> 00:36:18,478
Ben, just, um...

665
00:36:18,513 --> 00:36:19,881
Uh, please come in.

666
00:36:19,914 --> 00:36:21,381
Show me the rest
of the house, please.

667
00:36:21,415 --> 00:36:24,217
Okay. Okay, go ahead.

668
00:36:24,251 --> 00:36:26,386
Our intuitions are
more perceptive

669
00:36:26,420 --> 00:36:28,623
than our conscious minds.

670
00:36:30,925 --> 00:36:33,427
-Ben thinks I'm crazy.
-Huh!

671
00:36:35,797 --> 00:36:38,298
I've been called crazy
many times.

672
00:36:43,270 --> 00:36:45,873
Spiritual anomalies
often manifest themselves

673
00:36:45,907 --> 00:36:50,377
subconsciously as
an abiding sense of wrongness.

674
00:36:55,382 --> 00:36:57,785
And persistent unease.

675
00:36:57,819 --> 00:36:59,987
That's what I've been feeling.

676
00:37:02,422 --> 00:37:04,659
Was this room always an office?

677
00:37:04,692 --> 00:37:06,326
Yes.

678
00:37:06,359 --> 00:37:08,361
As long as we've lived here.

679
00:37:08,395 --> 00:37:10,397
It's Ben's.

680
00:37:10,430 --> 00:37:14,001
Although sometimes,
we use it as a guest room.

681
00:37:14,035 --> 00:37:17,437
There's very powerful energy
in this room.

682
00:37:35,388 --> 00:37:38,693
Someone who lived in here
experienced something terrible.

683
00:37:38,726 --> 00:37:40,695
It's me.

684
00:37:40,728 --> 00:37:42,462
I'm experiencing
something terrible.

685
00:37:42,496 --> 00:37:43,698
Can we wrap it up?

686
00:37:47,802 --> 00:37:49,837
I'll need the whole family
to gather in the dining room.

687
00:37:49,871 --> 00:37:51,271
Okay.

688
00:37:56,511 --> 00:37:57,645
How much are you paying her?

689
00:37:57,678 --> 00:37:58,813
Of course,
she's drawing this out.

690
00:37:58,846 --> 00:38:00,782
Please, let her finish.

691
00:38:00,815 --> 00:38:02,650
What are we doing here?
Who is she?

692
00:38:02,683 --> 00:38:04,085
I'm Dr. Deborah Burr.

693
00:38:04,118 --> 00:38:06,654
-She's not a doctor.
-I am a doctor.

694
00:38:06,687 --> 00:38:08,421
I mean, she's not a real doctor.

695
00:38:08,455 --> 00:38:09,524
-Ben.
-Could we just hurry this up?

696
00:38:10,558 --> 00:38:11,826
Join hands, please.

697
00:38:16,463 --> 00:38:18,599
So we may attempt
to contact the presence

698
00:38:18,633 --> 00:38:19,901
in this house.

699
00:38:19,934 --> 00:38:22,003
O spirit

700
00:38:22,036 --> 00:38:23,403
who resides here,

701
00:38:23,436 --> 00:38:25,072
make your presence known to us.

702
00:38:27,508 --> 00:38:28,576
Give us a sign,

703
00:38:28,609 --> 00:38:29,544
let us know your name

704
00:38:29,577 --> 00:38:32,412
so that we may help you
to move on from this--

705
00:38:32,445 --> 00:38:33,815
Hi there!

706
00:38:34,982 --> 00:38:36,851
-How are you?
-Did you hear that?

707
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:42,023
Will you be my friend?

708
00:38:42,056 --> 00:38:45,593
I'm always looking
for a new friend.

709
00:38:45,626 --> 00:38:47,628
I know I just met you,

710
00:38:47,662 --> 00:38:52,465
-but I love you very much.
-Oh! There's your ghost.

711
00:38:52,499 --> 00:38:53,901
Someone left the TV on.

712
00:38:53,935 --> 00:38:56,103
Wait, no! Don't.

713
00:38:57,404 --> 00:38:59,106
Did you see that?

714
00:38:59,140 --> 00:39:02,143
There's kids,
there's a unicorn, did you...

715
00:39:02,176 --> 00:39:04,712
Oh, God, where did it go?

716
00:39:04,745 --> 00:39:06,013
Uh...

717
00:39:06,047 --> 00:39:07,815
Okay, I think we're done here.

718
00:39:07,849 --> 00:39:10,417
As you wish.

719
00:39:10,450 --> 00:39:11,886
I take Venmo.

720
00:39:18,526 --> 00:39:22,663
It's just...it's bad enough
you didn't tell me, but...

721
00:39:22,697 --> 00:39:24,464
in front of the kids?

722
00:39:26,133 --> 00:39:28,435
I thought you'd be at baseball.

723
00:39:28,468 --> 00:39:30,470
Oh, okay, so...

724
00:39:30,504 --> 00:39:32,173
Thought it'd be easier
to do it behind my back?

725
00:39:42,149 --> 00:39:45,186
Hello?

726
00:39:45,219 --> 00:39:46,821
What are you doing?

727
00:39:46,854 --> 00:39:50,558
The, um...the show
with the orange unicorn,

728
00:39:50,591 --> 00:39:51,592
the one that Dr. Burr summoned?

729
00:39:51,626 --> 00:39:53,895
My God.
She didn't summon anything.

730
00:39:53,928 --> 00:39:55,563
I searched everywhere,
and there's...

731
00:39:55,596 --> 00:39:57,531
there's no mention of it.

732
00:39:58,766 --> 00:40:00,968
It's just some forgotten
show from the '90s.

733
00:40:01,002 --> 00:40:02,970
Yeah, but there's nothing.

734
00:40:04,805 --> 00:40:07,041
I think I'm gonna
make some calls tomorrow.

735
00:40:07,074 --> 00:40:08,609
Calls? Who you gonna call?

736
00:40:08,643 --> 00:40:09,877
More psychics?

737
00:40:09,911 --> 00:40:12,179
Bring more kooks
to the house? Grace.

738
00:40:19,720 --> 00:40:20,922
What's goin' on?

739
00:40:33,701 --> 00:40:35,970
I feel like
we have a third child.

740
00:40:41,876 --> 00:40:43,476
What?

741
00:40:43,511 --> 00:40:45,846
We've always said
we wanted three kids.

742
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:50,885
And the gap between
Timothy and Derek...

743
00:40:50,918 --> 00:40:52,586
is...

744
00:40:52,620 --> 00:40:54,855
Are you kidding?

745
00:40:54,889 --> 00:40:55,923
You're kidding, right?

746
00:40:55,957 --> 00:40:57,224
You--you're saying
you have a kid

747
00:40:57,258 --> 00:40:59,060
that you don't remember having?

748
00:41:00,861 --> 00:41:03,164
Okay, this is--sorry,
you're actually starting

749
00:41:03,197 --> 00:41:04,065
to scare me a little bit.

750
00:41:04,098 --> 00:41:06,801
I know. I'm scared, too.
I'm really scared.

751
00:41:06,834 --> 00:41:08,501
-I'm, I'm ter--
-No, no, no, no, no.

752
00:41:08,536 --> 00:41:09,603
This has to stop, okay?

753
00:41:09,637 --> 00:41:11,172
-This is crazy.
-I know.

754
00:41:11,205 --> 00:41:14,075
I know that it is crazy.

755
00:41:14,108 --> 00:41:15,710
Please be here with me.

756
00:41:15,743 --> 00:41:18,512
I am here, I'm-I'm...
right here, okay?

757
00:41:19,947 --> 00:41:21,515
Where the hell are you?

758
00:41:26,620 --> 00:41:28,122
What the hell?

759
00:41:28,155 --> 00:41:29,657
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

760
00:41:29,690 --> 00:41:31,926
You're not listening to me!

761
00:41:39,066 --> 00:41:40,267
What's next, Grace?

762
00:41:40,301 --> 00:41:42,069
You gonna have
all the conspiracy photos

763
00:41:42,103 --> 00:41:43,671
on the wall
with all the strings?

764
00:41:43,704 --> 00:41:44,939
You saw the show.

765
00:41:44,972 --> 00:41:45,773
Did you or did you not
see the show?

766
00:41:45,806 --> 00:41:47,775
-Yes.
-Okay. So, then--then there's--

767
00:41:47,808 --> 00:41:49,944
there's nothing anywhere.

768
00:41:49,977 --> 00:41:52,013
-Explain that.
-Okay.

769
00:41:52,046 --> 00:41:53,214
Lemme get this straight.

770
00:41:53,247 --> 00:41:55,983
The imaginary unicorn from TV

771
00:41:56,017 --> 00:41:57,284
kidnapped our kid,

772
00:41:57,318 --> 00:41:58,452
erased our memories,

773
00:41:58,486 --> 00:42:00,321
the memories of all their
teachers and their friends,

774
00:42:00,354 --> 00:42:02,123
and then snuck into
a Social Security office

775
00:42:02,156 --> 00:42:04,225
and erased all that information,
too. Whoa!

776
00:42:04,258 --> 00:42:06,660
It's a busy unicorn.

777
00:42:06,694 --> 00:42:09,697
Ben, please...please...

778
00:42:09,730 --> 00:42:12,566
Is our real family
not enough for you, Grace?

779
00:42:18,205 --> 00:42:21,108
I-I-I give everything
to this family.

780
00:42:22,710 --> 00:42:25,179
I've given everything.

781
00:42:26,781 --> 00:42:27,948
I know, I'm...

782
00:42:35,289 --> 00:42:38,893
I just--I need you to...

783
00:42:38,926 --> 00:42:41,662
take the time to fix...

784
00:42:44,131 --> 00:42:46,700
whatever this is.

785
00:42:46,734 --> 00:42:47,935
Okay?

786
00:42:49,837 --> 00:42:52,006
Because if you bring our kids
into this again,

787
00:42:52,039 --> 00:42:53,307
our real kids,

788
00:42:53,340 --> 00:42:56,010
bring a scam psychic
into the house,

789
00:42:56,043 --> 00:42:57,344
we're gonna have
a much bigger problem.

790
00:42:57,378 --> 00:42:58,245
I can't be around you
right now, I can't.

791
00:42:58,279 --> 00:42:59,814
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

792
00:42:59,847 --> 00:43:01,982
Okay. Well,
the feeling is mutual.

793
00:43:06,921 --> 00:43:08,656
Hey.

794
00:43:08,689 --> 00:43:10,057
Hi, hi.

795
00:43:10,091 --> 00:43:11,692
No electronics, okay, sweetie?

796
00:43:11,725 --> 00:43:13,394
Let's put that away.

797
00:43:13,427 --> 00:43:16,230
What were you and Dad
fighting about?

798
00:43:18,232 --> 00:43:19,633
Nothing.

799
00:43:22,002 --> 00:43:24,939
Um...people can love
each other very much

800
00:43:24,972 --> 00:43:26,307
and still fight.

801
00:43:30,277 --> 00:43:33,981
-Can I ask you something?
-Yeah.

802
00:43:34,014 --> 00:43:39,019
Have you ever seen a show
with an orange unicorn?

803
00:43:39,053 --> 00:43:41,989
-No...
-Okay, good.

804
00:43:42,022 --> 00:43:44,725
If you ever see it,

805
00:43:44,758 --> 00:43:46,293
you turn it off,

806
00:43:46,327 --> 00:43:49,663
and you come tell me, okay?

807
00:43:49,697 --> 00:43:51,832
-Okay.
-Okay.

808
