1073
01:00:00,401 --> 01:00:02,103
This one's for you.

1074
01:00:03,804 --> 01:00:07,041
♪ I'm homesick
for the open spaces ♪

1075
01:00:07,074 --> 01:00:10,811
♪ Homesick for familiar places

1076
01:00:10,845 --> 01:00:17,218
♪ I wish I could just have
one tiny taste of bein' home ♪

1077
01:00:17,251 --> 01:00:19,086
Home, home, home!

1078
01:00:19,120 --> 01:00:22,089
♪ I'm homesick
for the old homestead ♪

1079
01:00:22,123 --> 01:00:25,893
♪ Homesick for my featherbed

1080
01:00:25,926 --> 01:00:32,233
♪ Before I lay down dead,
I want to hang my hat at home ♪

1081
01:00:38,939 --> 01:00:43,277
♪ I'm homesick
but so far away ♪

1082
01:00:43,310 --> 01:00:47,148
♪ Homesick,
waiting for that day ♪

1083
01:00:47,181 --> 01:00:48,983
♪ A walking stick

1084
01:00:49,016 --> 01:00:54,822
♪ Please, let me get back
to my simple home

1085
01:00:54,855 --> 01:00:56,357
Flowers.

1086
01:01:11,038 --> 01:01:12,439
Wade?

1087
01:01:12,473 --> 01:01:14,708
Why'd you drop me, Freddy?

1088
01:01:14,742 --> 01:01:17,044
I'm sorry.

1089
01:01:17,077 --> 01:01:19,013
You killed me.

1090
01:01:19,046 --> 01:01:22,449
I was just so...scared.

1091
01:01:22,483 --> 01:01:24,919
You should be. You're weak.

1092
01:01:24,952 --> 01:01:26,487
Without me,
you're all gonna die.

1093
01:01:27,788 --> 01:01:29,089
I see you!

1094
01:02:01,088 --> 01:02:02,189
Strappy?

1095
01:02:08,128 --> 01:02:09,496
Where's Strappy?

1096
01:02:11,432 --> 01:02:13,400
Strappy?

1097
01:02:13,434 --> 01:02:15,869
Strappy!

1098
01:02:15,903 --> 01:02:17,838
Strappy's missing!

1099
01:02:17,871 --> 01:02:21,175
We'll find him, don't worry.

1100
01:02:23,310 --> 01:02:25,045
Strappy!

1101
01:02:25,079 --> 01:02:27,414
Strappy, where are you?

1102
01:02:27,448 --> 01:02:30,818
-Strappy!
-Strappy!

1103
01:02:30,851 --> 01:02:32,853
Strappy, where are you?

1104
01:02:32,886 --> 01:02:34,288
Is anything else missing?

1105
01:02:39,893 --> 01:02:41,228
They took him!

1106
01:02:41,262 --> 01:02:43,397
For the candy.

1107
01:02:43,430 --> 01:02:45,032
Come on! We need to go!

1108
01:02:50,437 --> 01:02:53,073
Wouldn't it be better to just
get help in Diamond City?

1109
01:02:53,107 --> 01:02:55,476
I'm sure they have policemen
and everything.

1110
01:02:55,510 --> 01:02:59,079
Yeah, we're so close, and...

1111
01:02:59,113 --> 01:03:01,282
they can help us
get Strappy back.

1112
01:03:04,251 --> 01:03:05,886
No.

1113
01:03:05,919 --> 01:03:07,522
I left Wade behind.

1114
01:03:07,555 --> 01:03:09,423
I'm not leaving
Strappy behind, too.

1115
01:03:09,456 --> 01:03:10,858
But aren't you scared?

1116
01:03:10,891 --> 01:03:11,892
Of course I'm scared!

1117
01:03:11,925 --> 01:03:14,862
You've gotta be scared
to be brave. Remember?

1118
01:03:14,895 --> 01:03:17,965
Isn't that what
the dumb song's all about?

1119
01:03:22,537 --> 01:03:23,904
Fine.

1120
01:03:23,937 --> 01:03:25,205
I'll go by myself.

1121
01:03:28,909 --> 01:03:31,979
Fuck! That is good!

1122
01:03:32,012 --> 01:03:34,616
Oh, oh, that's good!

1123
01:03:34,649 --> 01:03:36,283
We have seven left.

1124
01:03:36,317 --> 01:03:38,952
We can each have one a week
for three weeks

1125
01:03:38,986 --> 01:03:40,921
and then share the last one.

1126
01:03:40,954 --> 01:03:43,490
-It's not right to steal.
-Shut up, backpack!

1127
01:03:43,525 --> 01:03:45,627
Or we'll put you in the swamp.

1128
01:03:49,531 --> 01:03:51,599
Why...

1129
01:03:51,633 --> 01:03:54,602
I forgot how good
apple juice tasted.

1130
01:03:54,636 --> 01:03:56,270
Like fine wine.

1131
01:03:56,303 --> 01:03:58,972
Sip, George! Sip.

1132
01:03:59,006 --> 01:04:01,041
Make it last.

1133
01:04:01,075 --> 01:04:03,277
Uh...uh, guys?

1134
01:04:03,310 --> 01:04:04,546
What'd I just say?

1135
01:04:04,579 --> 01:04:07,181
George, put him in the swamp.

1136
01:04:07,214 --> 01:04:08,349
Oh, shit!

1137
01:04:10,017 --> 01:04:12,953
Hi, Buddy!
Didn't hear you comin'.

1138
01:04:12,986 --> 01:04:16,056
Well, that's all the time
we have.

1139
01:04:16,090 --> 01:04:19,426
♪ You love Buddy, yes you do

1140
01:04:19,460 --> 01:04:23,464
♪ And I love each one of you

1141
01:04:23,497 --> 01:04:27,535
♪ We're together happily

1142
01:04:27,569 --> 01:04:30,304
-Happily!
-♪ We'll always be best...

1143
01:04:30,337 --> 01:04:33,006
-Happily!
-Oh, the words aren't coming up.

1144
01:04:33,040 --> 01:04:35,242
-Happy!
-I guess you're too old!

1145
01:04:35,275 --> 01:04:36,977
Happy!

1146
01:04:37,010 --> 01:04:38,479
Happy!

1147
01:04:40,047 --> 01:04:41,583
George! No!

1148
01:04:41,616 --> 01:04:43,484
Where are they, Willie?

1149
01:04:43,518 --> 01:04:45,119
In the prairie,

1150
01:04:45,152 --> 01:04:46,286
out of their gourds,

1151
01:04:46,320 --> 01:04:48,122
probably still asleep.

1152
01:04:50,124 --> 01:04:51,392
-Thanks, pal.
-No, please! Please!

1153
01:04:51,425 --> 01:04:52,627
I've always loved ya.

1154
01:04:52,660 --> 01:04:55,396
I've always cared about ya
so much more than the others.

1155
01:04:55,429 --> 01:04:57,699
-Have a nice swim.
-Agh!

1156
01:05:09,611 --> 01:05:12,045
Hey, kids!

1157
01:05:12,980 --> 01:05:16,450
I have Strappy for you!

1158
01:05:16,483 --> 01:05:18,085
Leave him alone, Buddy!

1159
01:05:20,454 --> 01:05:22,456
Freddy!

1160
01:05:22,489 --> 01:05:24,425
I've missed you.

1161
01:05:24,458 --> 01:05:25,492
Freddy, no!

1162
01:05:25,527 --> 01:05:27,094
It's a trap! He--

1163
01:05:28,095 --> 01:05:29,731
Put him down!

1164
01:05:29,764 --> 01:05:32,232
We were just playing around.

1165
01:05:32,266 --> 01:05:35,436
It wasn't anything serious.

1166
01:05:35,469 --> 01:05:38,972
I'm here now,
so what do you want?

1167
01:05:39,006 --> 01:05:41,041
I just want a hug,

1168
01:05:41,074 --> 01:05:45,145
so we can end this episode
and start fresh.

1169
01:05:47,047 --> 01:05:50,217
You must be so tired of running.

1170
01:05:53,721 --> 01:05:55,389
-What the?
-Woo-hoo!

1171
01:05:55,422 --> 01:05:56,457
Get back here!

1172
01:05:56,490 --> 01:05:57,424
Come on!

1173
01:06:01,161 --> 01:06:05,332
That was so cool!

1174
01:06:06,400 --> 01:06:07,602
And brave,

1175
01:06:07,635 --> 01:06:09,336
like something Wade
would have done.

1176
01:06:10,805 --> 01:06:12,372
You were brave too.

1177
01:06:12,406 --> 01:06:14,174
We did it.

1178
01:06:14,208 --> 01:06:17,311
Of course,
friends stick together.

1179
01:06:17,344 --> 01:06:19,547
♪ Friends are forever ♪

1180
01:06:19,581 --> 01:06:20,748
It's okay, Hannah,

1181
01:06:20,782 --> 01:06:22,249
you don't need
to sing about it.

1182
01:06:24,485 --> 01:06:27,254
Diamond City, here we come!

1183
01:07:08,796 --> 01:07:11,465
Well, that's all the time
we have!

1184
01:07:15,637 --> 01:07:19,273
♪ You love Buddy,
yes you do ♪

1185
01:07:19,306 --> 01:07:23,110
♪ And I love each one of you

1186
01:07:23,143 --> 01:07:26,714
♪ We're together happily

1187
01:07:26,748 --> 01:07:30,585
♪ We'll always be best buddies

1188
01:07:30,618 --> 01:07:34,454
♪ I love every one of you

1189
01:07:34,488 --> 01:07:39,092
♪ I'm so glad you love me too

1190
01:07:48,570 --> 01:07:53,875
♪ He's a unicorn
from a magic land ♪

1191
01:07:53,908 --> 01:07:58,713
♪ And we call his name
when we need a hand ♪

1192
01:07:58,746 --> 01:08:02,850
♪ He's a pal
who knows our names ♪

1193
01:08:04,384 --> 01:08:08,590
♪ He's the king
of fun and games ♪

1194
01:08:10,157 --> 01:08:12,727
♪ It's Buddy,
oh, Buddy ♪

1195
01:08:12,760 --> 01:08:15,495
♪ He's cuddly, snuggly,
our best friend ♪

1196
01:08:15,530 --> 01:08:18,265
♪ It's Buddy,
oh, Buddy ♪

1197
01:08:18,298 --> 01:08:21,569
♪ He's huggy
and a little bit nutty ♪

1198
01:08:21,603 --> 01:08:23,705
♪ He teaches us
right from wrong

1199
01:08:23,738 --> 01:08:26,440
and makes it better
with a song ♪

1200
01:08:26,473 --> 01:08:29,209
♪ It's Buddy,
oh, Buddy ♪

1201
01:08:29,242 --> 01:08:31,546
♪ Our friend until the end

1202
01:08:31,579 --> 01:08:34,281
♪ It's Buddy ♪

1203
01:08:45,860 --> 01:08:46,794
I'm mad at you guys.

1204
01:08:46,828 --> 01:08:48,630
I'm not gonna share
my baseball with you.

1205
01:08:48,663 --> 01:08:49,731
What?

1206
01:08:49,764 --> 01:08:51,231
Oh, Buddy!

1207
01:08:51,933 --> 01:08:53,500
-Whoa!
-Buddy!

1208
01:08:54,902 --> 01:08:57,404
Hi there, Tyler.

1209
01:08:57,437 --> 01:08:59,439
Oh, what's wrong?

1210
01:08:59,473 --> 01:09:01,576
We were playing baseball,
but they hurt my feelings

1211
01:09:01,609 --> 01:09:03,310
by running away
when I was winning,

1212
01:09:03,343 --> 01:09:04,879
so now I don't want to play
with them.

1213
01:09:04,912 --> 01:09:07,749
But, Tyler,
these are our friends.

1214
01:09:07,782 --> 01:09:10,450
If they say they're sorry
for running away,

1215
01:09:10,484 --> 01:09:13,788
then it's important
to forgive them.

1216
01:09:13,821 --> 01:09:16,691
♪ Nobody's perfect

1217
01:09:16,724 --> 01:09:19,426
♪ We all make mistakes

1218
01:09:19,459 --> 01:09:21,461
♪ But it's important
to acknowledge

1219
01:09:21,495 --> 01:09:24,732
that apologies are great

1220
01:09:24,766 --> 01:09:26,333
But they didn't say sorry yet.

1221
01:09:26,366 --> 01:09:29,604
Kids, do you have
something to say?

1222
01:09:35,643 --> 01:09:37,411
We're sorry.

1223
01:09:37,444 --> 01:09:39,947
Yeah, sorry, uh...

1224
01:09:39,981 --> 01:09:41,214
Tyler.

1225
01:09:41,248 --> 01:09:43,283
Sorry, Tyler.

1226
01:09:43,316 --> 01:09:45,285
And what about you, Freddy?

1227
01:09:45,318 --> 01:09:48,556
Are you sorry
for running away?

1228
01:09:51,491 --> 01:09:54,327
Freddy, I can't hear you?

1229
01:09:57,665 --> 01:09:59,701
I'm sorry.

1230
01:09:59,734 --> 01:10:00,868
See?

1231
01:10:00,902 --> 01:10:03,370
Doesn't that feel good?

1232
01:10:03,403 --> 01:10:05,338
I accept your apology.

1233
01:10:05,372 --> 01:10:08,442
Now who's ready
for some baseball?

1234
01:10:08,475 --> 01:10:10,243
Yay!

1235
01:10:10,277 --> 01:10:12,880
Freddy, go to the nurse
while we warm up.

1236
01:10:12,914 --> 01:10:16,450
And come right back, okay?

1237
01:10:16,483 --> 01:10:17,719
Okay.

1238
01:10:29,564 --> 01:10:31,298
Hi.

1239
01:10:31,331 --> 01:10:32,734
I'm Nurse Grace.

1240
01:10:32,767 --> 01:10:34,301
I'm Freddy.

1241
01:10:34,334 --> 01:10:35,903
I like that name.

1242
01:10:35,937 --> 01:10:37,404
Have a seat, Freddy.

1243
01:10:41,341 --> 01:10:42,977
Oof.

1244
01:10:43,010 --> 01:10:44,846
That's a nasty cut.

1245
01:10:54,589 --> 01:10:57,424
Now, this might sting a little.

1246
01:10:57,457 --> 01:10:58,492
It's okay.

1247
01:11:02,063 --> 01:11:04,699
Did you get this cut
from a monster?

1248
01:11:06,934 --> 01:11:08,770
You know Buddy's a monster?

1249
01:11:11,105 --> 01:11:12,039
What?

1250
01:11:15,475 --> 01:11:16,511
I meant the...

1251
01:11:19,514 --> 01:11:22,415
Do you think Buddy's a monster?

1252
01:11:23,718 --> 01:11:25,052
I guess I'm just crazy.

1253
01:11:26,921 --> 01:11:28,990
I doubt that, Freddy.

1254
01:11:31,659 --> 01:11:34,695
Maybe it's the world
that's crazy.

1255
01:11:34,729 --> 01:11:37,098
Guess it's just better
to pretend everything's okay.

1256
01:11:37,131 --> 01:11:40,001
No, Freddy, that never works.

1257
01:11:43,403 --> 01:11:45,540
You have to trust yourself.

1258
01:11:47,074 --> 01:11:48,843
You used two.

1259
01:11:48,876 --> 01:11:50,611
So they can look out
for each other.

1260
01:11:55,448 --> 01:11:56,918
Batter up.

1261
01:11:56,951 --> 01:11:59,120
You ready, Freddy?

1262
01:12:08,696 --> 01:12:10,363
Bye, Nurse Grace.

1263
01:12:10,397 --> 01:12:11,431
Bye, Freddy Beans.

1264
01:12:20,373 --> 01:12:23,978
I'm so glad that everything
is back to normal

1265
01:12:24,011 --> 01:12:26,781
in time for our big game.

1266
01:12:26,814 --> 01:12:28,749
It makes me want to sing.

1267
01:12:28,783 --> 01:12:29,717
Yay!

1268
01:12:29,750 --> 01:12:33,020
Freddy, will you lead us
in our favorite song,

1269
01:12:33,054 --> 01:12:35,455
"Take Me Out to the Ballgame"?

1270
01:12:36,724 --> 01:12:39,627
Come on,
I know you know the words.

1271
01:12:53,774 --> 01:12:57,111
♪ I hate Buddy, yes I do

1272
01:12:57,144 --> 01:13:00,181
♪ I hate, I hate, I hate you

1273
01:13:00,214 --> 01:13:01,115
No!

1274
01:13:01,148 --> 01:13:03,651
What are you doing?

1275
01:13:03,684 --> 01:13:06,854
♪ Stab your heart
and kick your knee ♪

1276
01:13:06,888 --> 01:13:09,657
♪ Buddy, you're my enemy

1277
01:13:09,690 --> 01:13:12,193
♪ Get an axe,
chop off your head ♪

1278
01:13:12,226 --> 01:13:15,029
♪ I wish
you were fucking dead

1279
01:13:41,622 --> 01:13:44,025
I hate you too!

1280
01:13:44,058 --> 01:13:45,860
Get the hell away
from my daughter!

1281
01:13:57,605 --> 01:13:59,106
I found you, Freddy Beans.

1282
01:14:17,591 --> 01:14:19,060
Goodnight, Freddy Beans.

1283
01:14:19,093 --> 01:14:20,528
Goodnight, Mommy Beans.

1284
01:14:25,032 --> 01:14:25,933
Mom.

1285
01:14:32,974 --> 01:14:34,875
You have a mom?

1286
01:14:38,012 --> 01:14:39,046
Okay, okay, okay.

1287
01:14:39,080 --> 01:14:39,714
Okay.

1288
01:14:39,747 --> 01:14:40,414
Kids, get in the clubhouse.

1289
01:14:40,448 --> 01:14:42,616
Go, go, go, go, go, now, now.

1290
01:14:42,650 --> 01:14:44,085
What did you kids do?

1291
01:14:44,118 --> 01:14:45,219
Say you're sorry!

1292
01:14:45,252 --> 01:14:47,888
Say you love him
or we'll all die!

1293
01:14:51,625 --> 01:14:53,160
Are we still gonna
play baseball?

1294
01:14:56,063 --> 01:14:59,200
Um, help me move the couch,
okay?

1295
01:14:59,233 --> 01:15:00,601
Hey, what are you doing?

1296
01:15:00,634 --> 01:15:02,703
Hey, hey, hey,
what's the big idea?

1297
01:15:05,706 --> 01:15:07,742
Okay, all right, okay.

1298
01:15:09,810 --> 01:15:11,078
Mr. Mailbox!

1299
01:15:16,584 --> 01:15:18,319
It's okay.

1300
01:15:18,352 --> 01:15:21,022
You always loved
helping creatures, didn't you?

1301
01:15:21,055 --> 01:15:23,624
Do you remember your pet fish?

1302
01:15:23,657 --> 01:15:26,227
What was its name?

1303
01:15:26,260 --> 01:15:27,328
Fin.

1304
01:15:27,361 --> 01:15:28,863
Fin, yes.

1305
01:15:31,599 --> 01:15:32,767
We're all gonna die.

1306
01:15:32,800 --> 01:15:34,769
No, no, no, no,
it's okay, it's okay.

1307
01:15:34,802 --> 01:15:35,836
I am gonna get us out of here.

1308
01:15:35,870 --> 01:15:37,772
We tried.

1309
01:15:37,805 --> 01:15:39,173
There's nowhere to go.

1310
01:15:39,206 --> 01:15:41,776
Hey, if we got here,

1311
01:15:41,809 --> 01:15:43,044
if we got here,

1312
01:15:43,077 --> 01:15:44,745
we can get back home.

1313
01:15:44,779 --> 01:15:45,813
I know it.

1314
01:15:47,681 --> 01:15:49,750
It's okay, Mr. Mailbox.

1315
01:15:49,784 --> 01:15:51,185
Calm down.

1316
01:15:51,218 --> 01:15:52,686
It's okay.

1317
01:16:02,096 --> 01:16:05,332
Mr. Mailbox, you're a genius.

1318
01:16:05,366 --> 01:16:06,834
The Worry Well.

1319
01:16:06,867 --> 01:16:08,169
Magic things come from it.

1320
01:16:08,202 --> 01:16:09,637
Maybe it's a way out?

1321
01:16:09,670 --> 01:16:11,806
Yeah, okay,
that's our best shot.

1322
01:16:11,839 --> 01:16:15,042
Hey, where's the mailbox?

1323
01:16:15,076 --> 01:16:16,877
Should I just leave it
on the ground?

1324
01:16:25,152 --> 01:16:26,187
It's okay.

1325
01:16:30,791 --> 01:16:32,093
We're gonna be okay,
we're gonna be okay.

1326
01:16:32,126 --> 01:16:33,160
We're gonna be okay.

1327
01:16:51,879 --> 01:16:52,847
Buddy, no.

1328
01:16:52,880 --> 01:16:54,248
Buddy, we love you.

1329
01:16:54,281 --> 01:16:56,684
Kids, kids,
tell him you love him.

1330
01:16:56,717 --> 01:16:57,384
Tell him!

1331
01:17:01,288 --> 01:17:04,258
Couchy, Couchy,
tell Buddy you love him.

1332
01:17:06,794 --> 01:17:08,028
It's okay.

1333
01:17:08,062 --> 01:17:10,030
Buddy, don't be mad.

1334
01:17:10,064 --> 01:17:11,665
We all love you.

1335
01:17:11,699 --> 01:17:13,134
I promise we all love you.

1336
01:17:13,167 --> 01:17:15,169
No, Buddy, Buddy.

1337
01:17:23,777 --> 01:17:26,180
